  "comments": [
    {"at":0,"placement":"line","text":"Fills the 22 rows of 160 bytes of the map buffer with the cover character $7C."},
    {"at":30,"placement":"line","text":"Makes the table view_row_ptrs of the 24 visible character rows in the map buffer. Then puts the cover character $7C at a random place in each row, 48 times."},
    {"at":82,"placement":"side","text":"Random column 0-42."},
    {"at":89,"placement":"side","text":"cover_count is never 0 after the increment, so the next two instructions never run."},
    {"at":114,"placement":"line","text":"Fills the 256 bytes after the map buffer ($4DC3) and the 3 bytes before it ($4000) with the steel wall character $4A."},
    {"at":133,"placement":"line","text":"Draws one random cell of each cave row into the map buffer, in 69 passes. This uncovers the cave at random places."},
    {"at":177,"placement":"side","text":"Writes the cell code again. This draws the cell into the map buffer."},
    {"at":206,"placement":"line","text":"While cave_covered is set, rolls the cover character $7C up one pixel row each frame. It also plays the cover noise on voice 2 in a cycle of three frames."},
    {"at":291,"placement":"line","text":"Uncovers the cave: draws random cells, then draws all 22 rows of 40 cells into the map buffer, then fills the buffer border."}
  ],
